<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothar von Trotha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lothar von Trotha was a German general who commanded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">South West Africa</a> during the war against the Herero and Nama. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterberg">Battle of Waterberg</a> in 1904 he issued an extermination order against the Herero, driving them into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omaheke">Omaheke</a> desert, where many died of thirst. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> formally acknowledged the killings of the Herero and Nama as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> in 2021.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothar-von-trotha.jpg" alt="Lothar von Trotha" width="311" height="600" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lothar_von_Trotha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
